.TH SENTINEL-TUI 1 "March 2026" "Sentinel-CC v4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel-tui \- Sentinel-CC terminal dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel-loader
\-\-audit \-\-audit-format=json \fIBINARY\fR |
.B sentinel-tui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel-tui
reads JSON audit events from standard input and displays a live terminal
dashboard with aggregate counters, per-syscall breakdowns, and a scrolling
event tail.
.PP
It is designed to be piped from
.BR sentinel-loader (1)
running in JSON audit mode. The dashboard refreshes once per second and
supports all event types: ALLOW, BLOCK, CFI-FAIL, NR-MISMATCH,
FORK-TRACK, and FEXIT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version string and exit.
.SH DISPLAY SECTIONS
.TP
.B Counters
Aggregate counts for each event type (ALLOW, BLOCK, CFI-OK, CFI-FAIL,
NR-MISMATCH, FORK, FEXIT) plus total events and events/second.
.TP
.B Per-Syscall Breakdown
Table showing allow/block/fexit counts per syscall number with resolved
names (write, read, mmap, etc.).
.TP
.B Recent Events
Scrolling tail of the most recent events with color-coded actions:
green for ALLOW, red for BLOCK/CFI-FAIL, cyan for FORK, yellow for FEXIT.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Live dashboard for a protected binary
sudo sentinel-loader --audit --audit-format=json ./victim_phase2 | sentinel-tui

# With fexit return value tracking
sudo sentinel-loader --audit --fexit --audit-format=json ./myapp | sentinel-tui

# Replay from a log file
cat audit.jsonl | sentinel-tui
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sentinel-loader (1),
.BR sentinel-dump (1),
.BR sentinel-sign (1)
